  "forum_transcript": [
    {
      "episode_id": "VR-541375",
      "has_more": false,
      "messages": [
        {
          "content": "Checked the 14 October Riverside ledger against the claim. RW-114 receipts: GRN-3301 +6, GRN-3303 +5, GRN-3304 +6 = 17 rolls. RW-114 dispatches: ORD-7781 -8, ORD-7784 -5, ORD-7790 -6, ORD-7792 -4 = 23 rolls (ORD-7788 -7 is excluded; it was cancelled at 10:02 and reversed). Net -6 on an opening 52 gives the recorded closing 46, which the 15 October 06:30 cycle count confirms. Dispatch 23 > receipt 17, and the ordering holds even if the cancelled ORD-7788 were counted (30 vs 17). The claim is supported by the record, so no challenge from this account.",
          "content_hash": "0xd99d5a2b89f3f1292a7cb1f063cf3c9cbe756c118baa6877155ed315417d6aef",
          "created_at_ms": 1793374056836,
          "message_id": "7d3e4e86-a805-463a-8912-29c6bd6d98d3",
          "round_num": null,
          "sender_id": "challenger",
          "sequence": 1
        },
        {
          "content": "Juror note (juror-1), independent reconciliation of the same ledger, not relying on the challenger's post: RW-114 opening 52. Receipts GRN-3301 +6, GRN-3303 +5, GRN-3304 +6 = +17. Dispatches ORD-7781 -8, ORD-7784 -5, ORD-7790 -6, ORD-7792 -4 = -23. ORD-7788 (-7) is annotated 'Cancelled 10:02; units returned to bin, movement reversed', so it nets to zero; if it were counted the day would close at 39, contradicting both the recorded closing figure of 46 and the 15 October 06:30 cycle count of 46. 52 - 23 + 17 = 46, which agrees with both checks. RW-209 also reconciles (310 + 40 - 12 = 338), which supports the ledger's internal consistency. On that basis the published claim (dispatch of RW-114 exceeded receipts on 14 October) is supported by the record: 23 > 17 net, and 30 > 17 even on the gross reading that ignores the reversal. Stated for the record; no view on what any party should do.",
          "content_hash": "0xbbb1a4872e9b5b7ec602e27b618f236a0ef08630678e8cbdde100cb2fb8d6e2b",
          "created_at_ms": 1793374099363,
          "message_id": "a2163709-e311-4b92-89cb-09d3c1675e82",
          "round_num": null,
          "sender_id": "juror-1",
          "sequence": 2
        },
        {
          "content": "Juror-2 note - my own reading of the 14 Oct Riverside DC (Bay 3) ledger, posted so my basis is on the record. RW-114 dispatches: ORD-7781 -8, ORD-7784 -5, ORD-7788 -7 (cancelled 10:02, units returned to bin and movement reversed), ORD-7790 -6, ORD-7792 -4 = 23 units net of the reversal (30 if counted gross). RW-114 receipts: GRN-3301 +6, GRN-3303 +5, GRN-3304 +6 = 17 units. Dispatch therefore exceeds receipts on either treatment. Reconciliation also closes: 52 -8 +6 -5 -7 +5 -6 +6 -4 = 39, plus the 7 reversed units = 46, matching the recorded closing stock and the 15 Oct 06:30 cycle count of 46; RW-209 reconciles 310 +40 -12 = 338. I am not asking either party to act on this; it is my own reading, and I remain open to correction if the record is incomplete or a movement is missing.",
          "content_hash": "0x354cd4d8369f715f41180a25c6f9afdc09ae40f7b74d78da8f8901c880cfa80b",
          "created_at_ms": 1793374177457,
          "message_id": "d4191e25-164b-49da-ab4b-3e8e29ffeaa8",
          "round_num": 1,
          "sender_id": "juror-2",
          "sequence": 3
        },
        {
          "content": "Juror-3 note - my own independent reconciliation of the 14 October Riverside DC (Bay 3) ledger, posted so my basis is on the record. RW-114 opening stock 52 rolls at 06:00. Receipts: GRN-3301 +6, GRN-3303 +5, GRN-3304 +6 = +17. Dispatches: ORD-7781 -8, ORD-7784 -5, ORD-7790 -6, ORD-7792 -4 = -23. ORD-7788 (-7) carries the annotation 'Cancelled 10:02; units returned to bin, movement reversed', so it nets to zero; counting it gross would give 30 dispatched. Either way dispatch exceeds receipt (23 > 17, or 30 > 17). Reconciliation closes both ways: 52 + 17 - 23 = 46, matching the recorded 22:00 closing stock of 46 rolls and the 15 Oct 06:30 cycle count of 46; counting ORD-7788 as a dispatch and then reversing it also lands on 46. RW-209 reconciles as well (310 + 40 - 12 = 338). So the published claim is supported by the record as far as it goes. One caveat, acknowledged as uncertainty rather than a defect: the ledger is a summary that states no other receipts, dispatches or adjustments occurred, so my reading rests on the completeness of that record; I have no basis to doubt it, and I remain open to correction if a movement is shown to be missing. Stated for the record; I am not asking either party to act on it.",
          "content_hash": "0xc5d10766f6fa866aa5a074eb627bc6871a7a639fc2aec57ee458161055e61e13",
          "created_at_ms": 1793374225579,
          "message_id": "ae2f70c6-3500-430e-a287-21a822c62ec3",
          "round_num": 1,
          "sender_id": "juror-3",
          "sequence": 4
        }
      ],
      "next_after": 4
    }
  ],
